add_claim("THE TRAINING-GROUND CORNER ROUTINE, corroborated a second time: 'The easiest way to score on corners is **do not move the arrow, strong power lob to your defender, short header to nearest open man for tap in.** Granted free kicks take some skill now because of the angle but corners are easy.' So the simplest routine - leave the arrow alone - is also a recommended one.", 3, "setpieces/training-ground-corner-routine", [e_cd])
add_claim("THE PER-MOVE BEST-USE TABLE, consolidated: **Rainbow Flick = lift the ball over a defender** (use when an opponent is close) · **Feint = change direction** (use inside the box to trick defenders) · **Roulette = shield and turn** · **Bicycle/Scorpion Kick = finish crosses** · **Heading = headers and clears** · **Rabona = fancy cross**. The corpus had the inputs; this is the use case for each.", 3, "skillmoves/per-move-best-use-table", [e_dc] if False else [e_cd])
add_claim("THE COMBINATION TIP: '**Combine Close Control + Knock Ahead for tight-then-fast movement.**' So the two DLS25/26 additions are a PAIR - close control to hold the ball in traffic, then knock ahead to escape it - rather than two separate tools to be used independently.", 3, "skillmoves/close-control-plus-knock-ahead", [e_cd])
add_claim("THE HOLD-THE-BALL TACTIC, a third voice on the dribbling-while-stopped strategy: 'dribbling/holding the ball a little bit when you are on an attack and **cannot see well-positioned teammates to pass to.**' So possession is the correct play when the pass is not there - which is the same conclusion as the corpus's no-blind-passes rule, arriving from the other direction.", 3, "matchcraft/hold-the-ball-when-no-pass", [e_cd])
add_claim("A CROSS-DOMAIN CORROBORATION of the corpus's planted-foot read, from real-football coaching rather than DLS: '**Attack the Defender's Front Foot.** Defenders always have a slightly weaker side' and 'elite players target that moment of imbalance, and players trained to scan for the defender's raised foot and move toward it have a **35% higher success rate** in beating defenders.' **A real-football mechanism behind a DLS observation - recorded as corroboration, not as DLS evidence.**", 3, "errata/planted-foot-cross-domain-corroboration", [e_cd], notes="Explains WHY the DLS planted-foot read works")
